From 1680ba1e498a31828d9300fec48966817b83d195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:02:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MT-AXISLOCK + MT-ALMRST + HMI-KEEP-2: Motor Test axes are
 independent; Alarm Reset of the selected axis; the HMI keeper also runs while
 a box waits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260929: "只要某一軸alarm 就不讓我控制嗎? ... 每個軸都是獨立可控的, 其他如果有一樣方式被鎖的 一樣都要by 單軸,
然後我需要有alarm reset的按鈕在介面上 並且要有實際功能".

- MotorAccessMovingOf: ERROR_STOP / DISABLE are stopped states (golden MotionDone == READY made one alarmed axis lock
  every axis for ever); an active HOME job counts as moving on its own axis.
- MotorAccessAxisLock + runtime lock.motors / lock.perAxis: the page disables MoveN/MoveP/LoopMove only when the
  SELECTED axis moves (JOG / HOME / command sent / non-READY state). Non-1203 rows keep golden's page lock.
- JobsBusyWhy, HOME's loop cancel, LoopMove's home cancel, the servo toggle's AllBtnUp and the speed bar's
  bSingleHome now act on the same axis only. A LoopMove on another axis while one loops is refused with a clear
  message (one loop at a time) instead of a "looping" ack for the other axis.
- resetAlarm (new action, button btnAlarmReset): Acm_AxResetError on the selected 1203 axis (golden
  MotOutputOn's bAlarm branch). Moves nothing, does not servo-ON.
- wb_serve: W906_HmiKeeperTick also runs in the modal wait tick (5 s, Chrome, W906_HMI_URL); MODAL-WAKE stays
  as the fallback.
- tests: test_web_motor_access 545 passed / 0 failed (scratch build); test_webcmdguard list + resetAlarm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
